# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The package provides two ways to look at a shaded lightcone:\n"
msgstr "Le paquet offre deux façons d'observer un cône de lumière ombré :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`draw_shaded_lightcone` overlays the bounds onto the circuit diagram. THis is best for circuits on a 1D\n"
"chain of qubits, where the circuit diagram and the physical layout agree.\n"
msgstr ""
"`draw_shaded_lightcone` superpose les bornes au diagramme du circuit. C'est idéal pour les circuits sur une chaîne 1D\n"
"de qubits, où le diagramme du circuit et la disposition physique concordent.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`animate_shaded_lightcone` projects the bounds onto the QPU's coupling map and steps through the\n"
"circuit layer by layer. This is best when the qubit connectivity is more than a 1D line, where a circuit\n"
"diagram stops conveying which qubits are neighbors.\n"
msgstr ""
"`animate_shaded_lightcone` projette les bornes sur la carte de couplage du QPU et parcourt le\n"
"circuit couche par couche. C'est idéal lorsque la connectivité des qubits dépasse une simple ligne 1D, là où un diagramme\n"
"de circuit ne montre plus quels qubits sont voisins.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both visualizations show the same underlying numbers. This guide covers what those numbers mean, and explains the details\n"
"that are easy to misread.\n"
msgstr ""
"Les deux visualisations montrent les mêmes nombres sous-jacents. Ce guide explique ce que ces nombres signifient et détaille les points\n"
"faciles à mal interpréter.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Configuration {#setup}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the same Trotterized Ising circuit and observable as the [quickstart guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart).\n"
msgstr "Utilise le même circuit d'Ising trotterisé et la même observable que le [guide de démarrage rapide](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart).\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "`draw_shaded_lightcone` {#draw_shaded_lightcone}"
msgstr "`draw_shaded_lightcone` {#draw_shaded_lightcone}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each noisy box is shaded by the bound on the errors occurring there: bright means a large bound, and\n"
"a box fading into the background means its errors have little effect on the observable. Those faded\n"
"boxes are the candidates for dropping from the mitigated noise model.\n"
msgstr ""
"Chaque boîte bruitée est ombrée selon la borne des erreurs qui s'y produisent : brillante signifie une grande borne, et\n"
"une boîte qui s'estompe dans l'arrière-plan signifie que ses erreurs ont peu d'effet sur l'observable. Ces boîtes\n"
"estompées sont les candidates à l'exclusion du modèle de bruit atténué.\n"

